Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:09:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] cuda flashnext: the dense hyper-connection mix a warp a
 32-column group, eight groups a block

fn_hc_dense_mix ran one 32-thread block a (row, 32-column group): 80 blocks of one warp a row at 2,560
dims. fn_hc_dense_mix8 runs the same per-value ops and the same in-order group sum with eight groups a
256-thread block, so its bytes are fn_hc_dense_mix's.

Contract: fn_hc_dense_mix8 replaces fn_hc_dense_mix (8 shapes bit-equal, nonfinite rule stated,
repeat); its bound adds the kernel's bf16 roundings of each term and the mean. Control: the same
kernel with its inputs swapped, red at shapes.

GB10, FP4-Local, 4,096-row prompt chunks, no drafts: replies identical to main on the 8k and 32k
prompts; TTFT within run-to-run noise (8k 4.37-4.78 s vs 4.21-4.84 s, 32k 18.0 vs 17.9-18.8 s).

(cherry picked from commit c580159661e40e4bddb952446c9407271daf5409)
